# Close-out M1-G4 (failure origin): verdict.Assemble is the ONE place signals.failure_origin is written, and it must write it on EVERY unknown (the platform bills on it; a missing key is read as undetermined, i.e. free). The fault stops writing the key for one reason (greylisted): the sweep over the whole reason vocabulary must find the unknown that carries no key. In-memory, no database. The unpatched control passes.
GATE=m1-origin-assembler
TARGET=module:coldmail-verify
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestAssemble_EveryUnknownReasonCarriesAFailureOrigin (the sweep over every reason in the vocabulary)
CMD=cd control-plane && GOTOOLCHAIN=local go test -count=1 -v -run '^TestAssemble_EveryUnknownReasonCarriesAFailureOrigin$' ./internal/verdict/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestAssemble_EveryUnknownReasonCarriesAFailureOrigin
MESSAGE=signals has no string failure_origin
